  "id": "DrugBank_DB00521 - MONDO_5338",
  "verbalization": "Carteolol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Open-angle Glaucoma through a chain of indications that link it to ocular hypertension, a condition that is a known risk factor for the disease. The evidence suggests that Carteolol may exert a protective or modulatory effect on the eye, as it is associated with ocular hypertension, which in turn is linked to Open-angle Glaucoma. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple indirect pathways, each involving different medications that are indicated for ocular hypertension, and all ultimately leading to Open-angle Glaucoma. The shared indication of ocular hypertension across these pathways implies a potential mechanism by which Carteolol could influence ocular physiology, possibly through effects on intraocular pressure or other ocular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of ocular hypertension as a potential intermediate step in the relationship between Carteolol and Open-angle Glaucoma, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
